<section id="emergency-kit" aria-labelledby="emergency-kit-heading" class="content-defer border-b border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 items-center">
            <div class="lg:col-span-6 space-y-4">
                <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-blue-600">02 • Two-Key Protection Model</p>
                <h2 id="emergency-kit-heading" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">
                    How Your Emergency Secret Key Protects New Devices
                </h2>
                <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                    When you create a PassKee account, your browser generates a high-entropy 128-bit <strong>Emergency Secret Key</strong> alongside your Master Password. Together, they form a mathematical dual lock:
                </p>

                <ul class="space-y-3.5 pt-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                        <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 text-xs font-bold">1</span>
                        <span><strong>Sign In on a New Device (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-slate-800">Sign In to PassKee</code>):</strong> Requires your Email Address, Master Password, and your 128-bit Emergency Secret Key (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-slate-800">PK-XXXX-...</code>). Even if someone steals your password via phishing, they cannot sign in from their device without your Secret Key.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                        <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 text-xs font-bold">2</span>
                        <span><strong>Quick Unlock in Active Session (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-slate-800">Unlock Session</code>):</strong> When signing in, check <em>"Remember Secret Key for quick unlock in this session"</em>. PassKee encrypts your Secret Key in isolated <code class="font-mono text-xs text-slate-800">sessionStorage</code> using Argon2id, so unlocking after a 15-minute inactivity lock requires only your Master Password.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="lg:col-span-6">
                @* Exact visual replica of the "Save Your Emergency Secret Key" step from Register.razor *@
                <div class="rounded-2xl sm:rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 sm:p-8 shadow-xl">
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-5">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-[11px] sm:text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-blue-600">GET STARTED</p>
                            <h3 class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Create PassKee Account</h3>
                        </div>
                        <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-600 text-white shadow-md shadow-blue-500/20 shrink-0">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-user-plus text-base" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/60 p-4 sm:p-6 space-y-3.5">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-emerald-800">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-lg sm:text-xl text-emerald-600 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-base sm:text-lg">Save Your Emergency Secret Key</h4>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
                            PassKee has generated your unique <strong>Emergency Secret Key</strong> on this device. You will need both your Master Password and this Secret Key to sign in.
                        </p>
                        <div class="space-y-2">
                            <div class="p-3 sm:p-3.5 bg-white rounded-xl border border-emerald-300/80 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-900 break-all font-semibold shadow-inner">
                                PK-NFT6-G4F7-LNRY-TJPU-V7GV-8K2M
                            </div>
                            <div class="inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-white/90 border border-slate-200/80 px-3 py-2 text-xs font-medium text-slate-700">
                                <i class="fa-regular fa-copy mr-1.5" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                <span>Copy Secret Key</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/80 p-3 text-xs text-amber-800 flex items-start gap-2.5">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation text-amber-600 mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span><strong>Keep this safe!</strong> PassKee cannot recover or reset your Secret Key. If lost, your vault cannot be unlocked on new devices.</span>
                        </div>

                        <div class="pt-1 flex items-center gap-2.5">
                            <span class="flex h-4 w-4 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded bg-blue-600 text-white text-[10px]">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </span>
                            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-slate-700">
                                I have saved my Secret Key and understand PassKee cannot recover it.
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <a href="/registration" class="inline-flex w-full items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-600 px-4 py-3 text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right-to-bracket mr-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span>Continue to Sign In</span>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
